{
  "title": "Etiquettes of Travel",
  "data": "Setting Out\nBefore a journey, it is recommended to fast on Wednesday, Thursday and Friday, and to set out on a Saturday, Tuesday or Thursday.\nAvoid setting out on a Monday or a Wednesday, or on a Friday before noon.\nAvoid setting out on the 3rd, 5th, 13th, 16th, 21st, 24th and 25th of a lunar month, in the last nights of the month when the moon is not seen, and when the moon is in Scorpio.\nIf you must travel at such a time, recite the duas of travel and give charity, then set out when you wish.\nBefore setting out, perform ghusl, gather your family, pray two units and ask Allah for what is best. Recite [Ayat al-Kursi](A4), praise Allah, send blessings on the Prophet and his family, and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْتَوْدِعُكَ الْيَوْمَ نَفْسِيْ وَاَهْلِيْ وَمَالِيْ وَوُلْدِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASTAWDI'UKAL YAWMA NAFSEE WA AHLEE WA MAALEE WA WULDEE\nO Allah, on this day I entrust to You my self, my family, my property, my children,\nوَمَنْ كَانَ مِنِّيْ بِسَبِيْلٍ الشَّاهِدَ مِنْهُمْ وَالْغَاۤئِبَ\nWA MAN KAANA MINNEE BISABEELINISH SHAAHIDA MINHUM WAL GHAA'IB\nand everyone who is in my care, the present among them and the absent.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ احْفَظْنَا بِحِفْظِ الْاِيْمَانِ وَاحْفَظْ عَلَيْنَا\nALLAAHUMMAH FAZNAA BIHIFZIL EEMAANI WAHFAZ A'LAYNAA\nO Allah, protect us with the protection of faith, and keep watch over us.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا فِيْ رَحْمَتِكَ وَلَا تَسْلُبْنَا فَضْلَكَ اِنَّاۤ اِلَيْكَ رَاغِبُوْنَ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LNAA FEE RAHMATIKA WA LAA TASLUBNAA FADLAKA INNAA ILAYKA RAAGHIBOON\nO Allah, place us within Your mercy and do not deprive us of Your favour; we turn to You in longing.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا نَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ وَعْثَاۤءِ السَّفَرِ وَكَاٰبَةِ الْمُنْقَلَبِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA NA'OODHU BIKA MIN WA'THAA'IS SAFARI WA KA-AABATIL MUNQALAB\nO Allah, we seek Your protection from the hardships of travel, from a sorrowful return,\nوَسُوْۤءِ الْمَنْظَرِ فِي الْاَهْلِ وَالْمَالِ وَالْوَلَدِ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWA SOO'IL MANZARI FIL AHLI WAL MAALI WAL WALADI FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nand from finding harm in our family, property and children, in this world and the Hereafter.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَتَوَجَّهُ اِلَيْكَ هٰذَا التَّوَجُّهَ طَلَبًا لِمَرْضَاتِكَ وَتَقَرُّبًا اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAWAJJAHU ILAYKA HAADHAT TAWAJJUHA TALABAN LIMARDAATIKA WA TAQARRUBAN ILAYK\nO Allah, I set out towards You on this journey, seeking Your pleasure and nearness to You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَبَلِّغْنِيْ مَاۤ اُؤَمِّلُهٗ وَاَرْجُوْهُ فِيْكَ وَفِيْۤ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA FABALLIGHNEE MAA U'AMMILUHOO WA ARJOOHU FEEKA WA FEE AWLIYAA'IKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Allah, grant me what I long for and hope for in You and in Your friends, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen bid your family farewell. At the door of your house, recite the [Tasbih al-Zahra](I9), then [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) to your front, your right and your left, and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِلَيْكَ وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيْ وَعَلَيْكَ خَلَّفْتُ اَهْلِيْ وَمَالِيْ وَمَا خَوَّلْتَنِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA ILAYKA WAJJAHTU WAJHEE WA A'LAYKA KHALLAFTU AHLEE WA MAALEE WA MAA KHAWWALTANEE\nO Allah, to You I turn my face, and in Your care I leave my family, my property and all that You have bestowed on me.\nوَقَدْ وَثِقْتُ بِكَ فَلَا تُخَيِّبْنِيْ\nWA QAD WATHIQTU BIKA FALAA TUKHAYYIBNEE\nI have put my trust in You, so do not disappoint me,\nيَا مَنْ لَا يُخَيِّبُ مَنْ اَرَادَهٗ وَلَا يُضَيِّعُ مَنْ حَفِظَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA YUKHAYYIBU MAN ARAADAHOO WA LAA YUDAYYI'U MAN HAFIZAH\nO He who does not disappoint whoever turns to Him, and does not let perish whomever He guards.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ وَاحْفَظْنِيْ فِيْمَا غِبْتُ عَنْهُ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WAHFAZNEE FEEMAA GHIBTU A'NH\nO Allah, send blessings on Muhammad and his family, and guard for me all that I leave behind,\nوَلَا تَكِلْنِيْۤ اِلٰى نَفْسِيْ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWA LAA TAKILNEE ILAA NAFSEE YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand do not leave me to myself, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) eleven times, and [Surah al-Qadr](A101), [Ayat al-Kursi](A4), [Surah al-Nas](A118) and [Surah al-Falaq](A117). Pass your hands over your whole body, give what charity you can, and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اشْتَرَيْتُ بِهٰذِهِ الصَّدَقَةِ سَلَامَتِيْ وَسَلَامَةَ سَفَرِيْ وَمَا مَعِيَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNISH TARAYTU BIHAADHIHIS SADAQATI SALAAMATEE WA SALAAMATA SAFAREE WA MAA MA'EE\nO Allah, with this charity I buy my safety, the safety of my journey and of all that is with me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ احْفَظْنِيْ وَاحْفَظْ مَا مَعِيَ وَسَلِّمْنِيْ وَسَلِّمْ مَا مَعِيَ\nALLAAHUMMAH FAZNEE WAHFAZ MAA MA'IYA WA SALLIMNEE WA SALLIM MAA MA'EE\nO Allah, guard me and what is with me, keep me and what is with me safe,\nوَبَلِّغْنِيْ وَبَلِّغْ مَا مَعِيَ بِبَلَاغِكَ الْحَسَنِ الْجَمِيْلِ\nWA BALLIGHNEE WA BALLIGH MAA MA'IYA BIBALAAGHIKAL HASANIL JAMEEL\nand bring me and what is with me to my destination, with Your fair and gracious conveyance.",
  "tabs": [
    "What to Take Along\nTake along a staff of bitter almond wood, and recite [Surah Al-Qasas](A32), verses 22-28:\nوَلَمَّا تَوَجَّهَ تِلْقَآءَ مَدْيَنَ قَالَ عَسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَنْ يَّهْدِيَنِىْ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(22)\nWA LAMMAA TAWAJJAHA TILQAAA-A MADYANA QAALA A’SAA RABBEE AYN YAHDEYANEE SAWAAA-AS SABEEL.\nAnd when he turned his face toward Midian, he said, ‘Maybe my Lord will show me the right way.’\nوَلَمَّا وَرَدَ مَآءَ مَدْيَنَ وَجَدَ عَلَيْهِ اُمَّةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ يَسْقُوْنَ  وَوَجَدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمُ امْرَاَتَيْنِ تَذُوْدٰنِ‌ ۚ قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُمَا‌ ؕ قَالَتَا لَا نَسْقِىْ حَتّٰى يُصْدِرَ الرِّعَآءُ‌ وَاَبُوْنَا شَيْخٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(23)\nWA LAMMAA WARADA MAAA-A MADYANA WAJADA A’LAYHE UMMATAM MENAN NAASE YASQOON, WA WAJADA MIN DOONEHEMUM RA-ATAYNE TAZOODAAN, QAALA MAA KHATBOKOMAA, QAALATAA LAA NASQEE HATTAA YUSDERAR RE-A’AA, WA ABOONAA SHAYKUN KABEER.\nWhen he arrived at the well of Midian, he found there a throng of people watering [their flocks], and he found, besides them, two women holding back [their flock]. He said, ‘What is your business?’ They said, ‘We do not water [our flock] until the shepherds have driven out [their flocks], and our father is an aged man.’\nفَسَقٰى لَهُمَا ثُمَّ تَوَلّٰٓى اِلَى الظِّلِّ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ لِمَاۤ اَنْزَلْتَ اِلَىَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيْرٌ‏(24)\nFASAQAA LAHOMAA SUMMA TAWALLAA ELAZ ZILLE FAQAALA RABBE INNEE LEMAA ANZALTA ELAYYA MIN KHAYRIN FAQEER.\nSo he watered [their flock] for them. Then he withdrew toward the shade and said, ‘My Lord! I am indeed in need of any good You may send down to me!’\nفَجَآءَتْهُ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا تَمْشِىْ عَلَى اسْتِحْيَآءٍ  قَالَتْ اِنَّ اَبِىْ يَدْعُوْكَ لِيَجْزِيَكَ اَجْرَ مَا سَقَيْتَ لَنَا‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهٗ وَقَصَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَصَصَ ۙ قَالَ لَا تَخَفْ‌ نَجَوْتَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(25)\nFA-JAAA-ATHO EHDAAHOMAA TAMSHEE A’LAS TEHYAAA, QAALAT INNA ABEE YADO’OKA LEYAJZEYAKA AJRA MAA SAQAYTA LANAA, FALAMMAA JAAA-AHU WA QASSA A’LAYHIL QASASA, QAALA LAA TAKHAF, NAJAWTA MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen one of the two women approached him, walking bashfully. She said, ‘Indeed my father invites you to pay you the wages for watering [our flock] for us.’ So when he came to him and recounted the story to him, he said, ‘Do not be afraid. You have been delivered from the wrongdoing lot.’\nقَالَتْ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا يٰۤاَبَتِ اسْتَاْجِرْهُ‌ اِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَاْجَرْتَ الْقَوِىُّ الْاَمِيْنُ‏(26)\nQAALAT EHDAAHOMAA YAA ABATIS TAAJIRHO, INNA KHAYRA MANIS TAAJARTAL QAWIYYUL AMEEN.\nOne of the two women said, ‘Father, hire him. Indeed the best you can hire is a powerful and trustworthy man.’\nقَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُنْكِحَكَ اِحْدَى ابْنَتَىَّ هٰتَيْنِ عَلٰٓى اَنْ تَاْجُرَنِىْ ثَمٰنِىَ حِجَجٍ‌ۚ فَاِنْ اَتْمَمْتَ عَشْرًا فَمِنْ عِنْدِكَ‌ۚ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اَشُقَّ عَلَيْكَ‌ؕ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(27)\nQAALA INNEE OREEDO AN UNKEHAKA EHDAB NATAYYA HAATAYNE A’LAA AN TAAJORANEE SAMAANEYA HEJAJ, FA-IN ATMAMTA A’SHRAN FAMIN I’NDEK, WA MAA OREEDO AN ASHUQQA A’LAYK, SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nHe said, ‘Indeed I desire to marry you to one of these two daughters of mine, on condition that you hire yourself to me for eight years. And if you complete ten, that will be up to you, and I do not want to be hard on you. God willing, you will find me to a righteous person.’\nقَالَ ذٰ لِكَ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكَ‌ ؕ اَيَّمَا الْاَجَلَيْنِ قَضَيْتُ فَلَا عُدْوَانَ عَلَىَّ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِيْلٌ‏(28)\nQAALA ZAALEKA BAYNEE WA BAYNAK, AYYAMAL AJALAYNE QAZAYTO FALAA U’DWAANA A’LAY, WAL LAAHO A’LAA MAA NAQOOLO WAKEEL.\nHe said, ‘This will be [by consent] between you and me. Whichever of the two terms I complete, there shall be no imposition upon me, and Allah is witness over what we say.’\nSet out wearing a turban with its end wound under the chin; it guards against theft, drowning and burning.\nTake along some of [the soil of Imam Husayn (a.s.)](AG21), and when you take it, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰذِهِ طِيْنَةُ قَبْرِ الْحُسَيْنِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ وَلِيِّكَ وَابْنِ وَلِيِّكَ اتَّخَذْتُهَا حِرْزًا لِمَا اَخَافُ وَمَا لَاۤ اَخَافُ\nALLAAHUMMA HAADHIHI TEENATU QABRIL HUSAYNI A'LAYHIS SALAAMU WALIYYIKA WABNI WALIYYIKAT TAKHADHTUHAA HIRZAN LIMAA AKHAAFU WA MAA LAA AKHAAF\nO Allah, this is soil from the grave of al-Husayn, peace be upon him, Your friend and the son of Your friend. I have taken it as a protection from what I fear and what I do not fear.\nTake along rings of agate and of turquoise. Best is a ring of yellow agate, engraved on one side with:\nمَا شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ اَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ\nMAA SHAA'ALLAAHU LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHI ASTAGHFIRULLAAH\nWhatever Allah wills. There is no strength save in Allah. I seek Allah’s forgiveness.\nand on the other side with:\nمُحَمَّدٌ وَعَلِيٌّ\nMUHAMMADUN WA A'LIYY\nMuhammad and Ali.\nFor the turquoise ring, Imam Ali al-Hadi (a.s.) taught this engraving, that of Amir al-Mu'minin's (a.s.) ring, on one side:\nاَللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ\nALLAAHUL MALIK\nAllah is the King.\nand on the other side:\nاَلْمُلْكُ لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ\nAL-MULKU LILLAAHIL WAAHIDIL QAHHAAR\nThe kingdom belongs to Allah, the One, the All-Subduing.",
    "On the Way\nRecite [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) every night of the journey, and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ مَسِيْرِيْ عِبَرًا وَصَمْتِيْ تَفَكُّرًا وَكَلَامِيْ ذِكْرًا\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'L MASEEREE I'BARAN WA SAMTEE TAFAKKURAN WA KALAAMEE DHIKRAA\nO Allah, make my journeying a lesson, my silence reflection, and my speech remembrance of You.\nFor protection, recite these words of Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.):\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ وَمِنَ اللّٰهِ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ وَفِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI WA MINALLAAHI WA ILALLAAHI WA FEE SABEELILLAAH\nIn the Name of Allah, and by Allah, and from Allah, and to Allah, and in the way of Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِلَيْكَ اَسْلَمْتُ نَفْسِيْ وَاِلَيْكَ وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيْ وَاِلَيْكَ فَوَّضْتُ اَمْرِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA ILAYKA ASLAMTU NAFSEE WA ILAYKA WAJJAHTU WAJHEE WA ILAYKA FAWWADTU AMREE\nO Allah, to You I have surrendered myself, to You I have turned my face, and to You I have entrusted my affairs.\nفَاحْفَظْنِيْ بِحِفْظِ الْاِيْمَانِ مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيَّ وَمِنْ خَلْفِيْ وَعَنْ يَمِيْنِيْ وَعَنْ شِمَالِيْ وَمِنْ فَوْقِيْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِيْ\nFAHFAZNEE BIHIFZIL EEMAANI MIN BAYNI YADAYYA WA MIN KHALFEE WA A'N YAMEENEE WA A'N SHIMAALEE WA MIN FAWQEE WA MIN TAHTEE\nSo guard me with the protection of faith, from in front of me and from behind me, from my right and from my left, from above me and from below me,\nوَادْفَعْ عَنِّيْ بِحَوْلِكَ وَقُوَّتِكَ فَاِنَّهٗ لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWADFA' A'NNEE BIHAWLIKA WA QUWWATIKA FA-INNAHOO LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nand defend me by Your might and Your power, for there is no might and no power save in Allah, the High, the Great.\nSay \"Bismillah\" whenever you mount or board.\nKeep your provisions and your money in a safe place.\nHelp your companions on the journey, and do not hold back from meeting their needs.\nTravel with companions who spend as you do.\nDo not drink the water of a new stopping place until you have mixed it with water from the one before.\nTake along some soil of your hometown. At each stop, put a little into the water you drink, stir it, and drink once it has settled and the water is clear.\nBe good-tempered and forbearing on the journey.\nTake good provisions, especially on the way to Makkah. On a journey to visit Imam Husayn (a.s.), avoid fine food such as roast meat and sweets.\nAbove all, keep your obligatory prayers: pray them at the start of their time with all their conditions, not riding, not with tayammum when wudu is possible, and not with impure body or clothes.\nAfter every shortened (qasr) prayer, recite 30 times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nGlory be to Allah, all praise is for Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest."
